<Layout
  title={"Satiation Benchmark: Reference Harness, Adapters, and Telemetry Attribution"}
  description={"About: Fixed sequential Rust reference harness (Lane B), multi-shape adapter bridge (Shapes D, M, H, I), C1-C12 conformance suite, and rootless L0-L4 telemetry attribution verified across Apple M5 Max, NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor (INA238/INA3221 measured_j), Framework AMD Strix Halo, and Intel Raptor Lake."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Satiation Benchmark: Reference Harness, Adapters, and Telemetry Attribution
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study specifies and empirically audits how diverse models and external coding agents take an identical fixed benchmark without conflating model capability with wrapper policy or conflating shared-host counters with physical rail joules. It pairs a deterministic Rust reference harness (`Lane B`) and a single loopback proxy bridge (`Shapes D, M, H, I`) with a twelve-check conformance suite (`C1`–`C12`) and a five-level rootless telemetry engine (`L0`–`L4` crossed with attribution labels `A1`–`N`), verified live across four silicon archetypes (`Apple M5 Max`, `NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor`, `Framework AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395`, and `Intel Core i9-13900H`).
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Cross-platform harness determinism and `C1`–`C12` conformance: all 12 Rust reference and OS confinement checks pass on Apple M5 Max, and all four silicon platforms (`arm64` macOS, `aarch64` Tegra Linux, `x86-64` AMD Zen 5, `x86-64` Intel Raptor Lake) reproduce the exact `1M`-record `DNULLMM1` `10k`-probe checksum (`15027705736`), zero-byte-diff `14`-turn `ContextRule_v0` + `Truncate_v0` replay (`149,747 B`, `SHA-256` `d697ed14...`), and `0.868–9.544 ms` `SIGKILL` process-tree cleanup (`< 2,000 ms` ceiling), alongside `24/24` and `6/6` completion parity between `Lane B` and `Shape H` (`Claude Code 2.1.330`, clearing `Falsifier 8` at `1.67×–3.44×` lower prompt+cache token volume).</li>
        <li>Empirical cloud non-determinism (`C12`): across 32 live `satb-proxy` calls (`8` identical requests per endpoint), `Anthropic claude-opus-5-5` and `claude-sonnet-5-5` reject `temperature = 0.0` with `HTTP 400` deprecation and emit `8/8` distinct raw outputs (`4` and `2` distinct algebraic identities), `Cerebras gpt-oss-120b` (`temperature = 0.0, seed = 42`) emits `2/8` distinct outputs, and `xAI grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning` emits `1/8` algebraic identity with `8/8` distinct explanations — whereas local `Shape D` (`dnull`) emits `1/8` bit-identical digest.</li>
        <li>Multi-host hardware rails (`measured_j` vs. `reported_j`), observer cadences, and `B`-vs-`C` falsifiers: on `NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor`, world-readable (`0444`) `TI INA238` (`VIN` `L1`) and `INA3221` (`ch1 VDD_GPU`, `ch2 VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS`, `ch3 VIN_SYS_5V0` `L2`/`L1`) record physical shunt `measured_j` (`2.95 ms` `I2C` read latency, `66.55 Hz` ceiling) and physically separate active co-tenant `LLM` `VDD_GPU` draw from `VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS`; on `Framework AMD Strix Halo`, `0440 root:energy` `udev` permissions enforce `PLATYPUS` sandbox `EACCES` isolation (`24.34 µs` `RAPL` reads, `94.28 Hz`, plus `0444` `amdgpu PPT` with `energy1_input` absent); on `Intel Core i9-13900H`, `0444` `RAPL` exposes `psys` (`L1`) and `package-0`/`core`/`uncore` (`L2`, `97.12 Hz`); and across all four hosts, `Step 7` sum checks hold (`0–1 µJ` residual) while `CPU`-proportional (`Kepler`, label `C`) splitting errs by `32.59%–73.62%` on sequential compute-plus-I/O runs (`Falsifier 3`).</li>
        <li>Not claimed: dedicated-host `A2` net placement energy (withheld across all four machines because co-tenant jobs were active during capture, `dedicated_host = false`, with `measured_j` and `reported_j` kept strictly separated and never summed), external `L0` wall-plug `AC` readings, closed-API server energy (`not_available`, label `N`; fleet sustainability medians never enter receipts), or integrated-GPU `NVML` cumulative energy on `Jetson AGX Thor` while the shared `GPU` lock was held.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

